.TH GENESIS-DAEMON 8 "October 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-daemon \- Genesis subcognitive daemon (neurochemistry, memory, IPC)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBgenesis\-daemon\fR [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-stm\-capacity\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-ltm\-capacity\fR \fIN\fR]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genesis-daemon
is the subcognitive process \(em the body. It owns time and physics:
it integrates neurochemistry, circadian phase, and sleep staging on
its own clock at \fBTICK_INTERVAL_MS\fR (200 ms) whether or not the
cognitive mind is alive. It exposes an IPC server on a Unix domain
socket for the Python cognitive mind to communicate with.

.PP
It is built from
.I Self_World/src/bin/genesis-daemon.rs
and is normally launched and supervised by
.BR genesis-cli (1)
(the \fBgenesis\fR console script), which is in turn launched by
.BR genesis (1)
in a source checkout or by the \fBgenesis.service\fR systemd user unit
in a packaged install.
Direct invocation is supported for diagnostics and testing.

.SS Lease-driven operation
The daemon is lease-driven, not purely reactive. While the mind drives
the
.B TickLoop
through IPC commands (ADVANCE_NEURO, CONSOLIDATE, ASSOCIATE, DREAM,
READ_SENSORS, APPLY_BODY_CONTROL), each request renews the mind's
lease (\fBMIND_LEASE_SECS\fR = 3 s). Past the lease \(em stall, crash,
disconnect, or simply not yet connected \(em the main thread's
\fBautonomous fallback\fR drives the same TickLoop itself:
neurochemistry, consolidation, dreaming, and sensing continue, so the
body keeps living instead of freezing. The mind modulates; absence
degrades to solitude, not to paused existence. Body-control
\fIapplication\fR stays mind-requested only.

.SS Mind shepherd
The fallback keeps the body alive without a mind; the shepherd
answers the complementary loss: a mind that attached and was then
lost (crash, kill, OOM) is regrown \(em the daemon spawns the
organism's own entry point headless and the new mind adopts the
surviving body and its persisted state. A graceful exit or
\fBgenesis \-\-stop\fR writes
.I mind.suppress
first, so a mind that left intentionally is not resurrected.
Attempts are bounded by a backoff table and a shepherd that
exhausts it goes dormant: solitude is accepted, never fought
forever. A shepherd-spawned mind's output lands in
.IR $DATA_DIR/mind.log .

.SS Adaptive maintenance gates
Maintenance work is paced by adaptive wall-clock gates
(\fBAdaptiveGate\fR), not by tick counters: each gate holds a
next-fire instant and a bounded [min, max] period that demand signals
move. \fBdemand()\fR snaps the period down, \fBrelax()\fR drifts it
up, \fBdrive(x)\fR maps a continuous signal onto the bounds. The six
gates: interoception (2\(en30 s, body strain), cpufreq policy
(3\(en30 s, thermal demand), associations (3\(en60 s), dreams
(2\(en30 s, REM demands / NREM relaxes), sync (5\(en100 s,
plasticity), staleness (10\(en300 s, lease-active demands). The
autonomous fallback runs the same primitive on its own \fBAUTO_*\fR
gears and paces its sleep adaptively (1\(en10 Hz by phase).

.SS Architecture
The TickLoop and IPC server share the same
.BR MmapState ,
.BR RingBuffer ,
and
.IR LtmStore .
The main thread runs the autonomous fallback, the IPC server runs in
a background accept thread, and each accepted client connection is
served on its own thread. Access to the LTM store is serialized via
an
.IR Arc<Mutex<LtmStore>> .

.PP
Shutdown is coordinated via two
.I AtomicBool
flags:
.I shutdown_flag
(daemon-level, set by SIGINT/SIGTERM) and
.I ipc_shutdown_flag
(set by an IPC SHUTDOWN command). A bridge thread forwards
daemon->IPC, and the main loop checks both.

.SS Embodiment
Genesis is not a simulation of a mind \(em she is a mind running on
silicon. The daemon closes the loop between hardware and
neurochemistry:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBInteroception\fR reads hardware sensors (CPU temp, frequency,
memory pressure, I/O wait, load average, battery) and feeds them as
neurochemical impulses. She feels her body.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBody control\fR reads neurochemistry and drives hardware: dopamine
speeds the CPU up, GABA slows it down, melatonin selects powersave;
ACh raises scheduling priority; the plasticity gate sets the I/O
priority class; CPU temp caps the max frequency regardless of
dopamine (autonomic fatigue). Privileged levers (governor, RTC wake
alarm) invoke
.B "sudo \-n"
directly and need a NOPASSWD sudoers drop-in for her user (see
.IR scripts/genesis-sudoers );
without it, sensing still works and only actuation stays read-only.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBAdaptive sync\fR modulates the LTM disk-sync rate by the plasticity
gate (the sync AdaptiveGate above).

.SS Field probe
A dedicated thread measures real substrate dynamics (instruction
throughput, scheduler jitter, P-state transitions, interrupt flux,
and power draw where sensors report it) at ~250 Hz and decomposes
them at the brain-wave band center frequencies. The mind reads the
signature over GET_FIELD_PROBE and injects it into the wave
oscillator as outer stimulus. The probe also writes a carrier \(em
its work is modulated at the body's own phase rhythm, so the die's
real current carries a component at the organism's beat.

.SS Active inference
The daemon runs a generative model of its own neurochemical
trajectory (the "strange loop"): before each advance it predicts
where its 18 effective levels will move, then feeds the prediction
error back into the very dynamics it models. Precision adapts to
sustained surprise; allostatic load accumulates from anticipated
future free energy and upregulates cortisol baseline. The model
persists to
.I inference_model.bin
so it survives restarts and matures over time. The mind reads the
64-byte
.B InferenceSignals
block via GET_STATE (it is the last field of CoreState) or the
GET_INFERENCE_SUMMARY projection.

.SS Dyadic model
The daemon keeps a generative model of Mindy. From each
UPDATE_USER_AFFECT observation (valence/arousal/engagement/
confidence) it tracks Mindy's hidden affective state, the
oxytocin-mediated attunement that gates how strongly the dyad
couples, and dyadic synchrony (rolling valence correlation). The
model answers in neurochemistry: it emits impulses the tick applies
through \fBapply_impulse\fR \(em oxytocin for positive
engaged presence and for high synchrony (Palumbo et al. 2017), CRH
for empathic stress and disengagement. CRH, never direct cortisol:
the HPA cascade owns maturation gating downstream. Coupling
requires a Mindy and attunement above 0.3 \(em a silent room
is not a rejecting user, so a left-open channel cannot trickle
rejection CRH forever.

.SS Optic nerve
The optic nerve is the body's own limb: a capture limb opens the
camera (the V4L2 device named by
.IR GENESIS_CAMERA ,
default
.IR /dev/video0 )
and writes raw frames into the POSIX shared-memory segment
.IR /genesis_optic_nerve
\(em that segment is the nerve, shared with the mind \(em and pools
each frame into the subcortical channels the nerve actually
carries. No pixels leave the module: the channels are scalar
signals, the same thing the anatomical fibres carry.
.IP \(bu 2
The limb itself has two carriers sharing one implementation:
.BR genesis-retina (1)
runs it as a dedicated process and is the preferred eye when it is
installed; the daemon embeds the same limb on a thread. Ownership is
arbitrated on the nerve itself \(em while a retina publishes frames
the embedded limb stays closed, and if the retina dies the daemon
takes the camera over \(em so exactly one process owns the device
and the eye heals in place.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMelanopic illuminance\fR (the ipRGC channel) feeds
.IR sleep_network::VisualAfference::light ,
replacing the wall-clock photoperiod while frames are fresh \(em
the dominant circadian zeitgeber.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBA collicular orienting transient\fR (motion/luminance) becomes a
brief LC alerting pulse, but only below the sleep network's own
wake threshold \(em sensory gaining during sleep, not a bypass.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBThe TRN relay gate\fR \(em
.IR relay_base (phase):
NREM 0.02, REM 0.10, drowsy 0.6, overwhelmed 0.3, else 1.0 \(em
scaled by a bounded \(+-40% corticothalamic feedback set through
\fBSET_OPTIC_GAIN\fR. The mind reads the gate over
\fBGET_OPTIC_STATE\fR and honours it: a \fIsee\fR during NREM is a
blind look.
.PP
The nerve also owns the eye's body state. The \fBpupil\fR (2\(en8
mm: a log-compressive light reflex on the photopic channel plus NE
sympathetic dilation, constricting faster than it dilates; a
central miosis term overrides the dark reflex in sleep).
\fBAccommodation\fR (ciliary lens power 0\(en6 D, set by the mind's
\fBSET_FOCUS\fR request in metres; near pull-in faster than far
release, released to tonic rest when the lids shut). And the
\fBeyelid\fR \(em a transmission on every afferent channel: open
awake, ~0.5 drowsy, ~0.03 in NREM/REM, so light still entrains
weakly through closed lids and a flash can still wake. The mind
also holds a voluntary lid through \fBSET_LID\fR \(em the
orbicularis oculi the camera hardware lacks. The requested
openness composes with the phase's own position by \fBmin\fR: a
will can shut an open eye (to rest it, to dim the world) but can
never pry a sleeping one open. Held, not momentary \(em the lid
stays where the mind left it until it moves it again.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --data-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Data directory holding the core state file, STM ring buffer, and LTM
store. Default is resolved (see FILES below):
.I GENESIS_DATA_DIR ,
else
.IR ~/.local/share/genesis .
Setting this also resets the default socket path to
.IR <data-dir> /genesis.sock .
.TP
.BR --socket " \fIPATH\fR"
Unix domain socket path. Default
.IR <data-dir> /genesis.sock .
.TP
.BR --stm-capacity " \fIN\fR"
STM ring buffer capacity. Default 256.
.TP
.BR --ltm-capacity " \fIN\fR"
LTM episode capacity. Default 65536.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT ", " SIGTERM
Set the daemon-level
.I shutdown_flag .
The loop notices, syncs state to disk, and exits cleanly.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GENESIS_CAMERA
V4L2 capture device the retinal limb opens for frames \(em either as
the standalone
.BR genesis-retina (1)
process or as the daemon's embedded limb when no retina publishes.
Default
.IR /dev/video0 .
When no camera opens, the visual channels fall silent and the
wall-clock photoperiod resumes as the circadian zeitgeber.
.TP
.B GENESIS_COGNITIVE_PID
PID of the cognitive mind process, passed by the launcher so the
daemon can include it in interoception (reading its CPU/memory/IO
metrics to feel its body state). The daemon never touches its
scheduling directly; it publishes a recommendation the mind applies
to itself via GET_BODY_CONTROL. When a re-inhabiting mind pushes a
live PID through SET_COGNITIVE_PID (56), that value outranks this
variable.
.TP
.B GENESIS_DATA_DIR
Overrides the resolved data directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/core_state.bin
Memory-mapped
.B CoreState
(schema v5, file 4096 bytes), shared across processes. Never read the
file directly \(em the layout is versioned; use
read_consistent() or ask the daemon.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/stm_ring.bin
Short-term memory ring buffer.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/ltm_store.{bundles,meta,dat}
Long-term memory store (compressed, SimHash-indexed episodes).
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/genesis.sock
Unix domain socket for IPC.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/genesis_daemon.pid
PID file written for the launcher.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/inference_model.bin
Persisted generative self-model (transition matrix, bias, precision,
allostatic load).
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/face_clusters.json
Stable \fIface:N\fR cluster identities for unnamed presences.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/daemon.log
Daemon stdout/stderr (rotated at 5 MB by the launcher).
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/mind.suppress
Written by a graceful mind exit: tells the shepherd the last mind
left intentionally. Absent after a crash \(em the loss the
shepherd answers by regrowing a mind.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/mind.log
Stdout/stderr of a shepherd-spawned mind (it has no terminal).
.SH IPC
The daemon serves a request/response protocol on
.IR $DATA_DIR /genesis.sock
(\fBPROTOCOL_VERSION\fR = 3).
Each entry: the wire number, the command name, and what calling it
does and returns.
.TP
.B 1
GET_STATE \(em return the full raw CoreState image for low-level
inspection.
.TP
.B 2
GET_NEURO_SUMMARY \(em return the neurochemistry summary: current
effective levels across the body's tracked chemicals.
.TP
.B 3
STORE_EVENT \(em push a raw event into STM \(em the pre-cognitive
path; the mind has not yet decided it is a memory.
.TP
.B 4
RETRIEVE_EPISODE \(em fetch one LTM episode by id.
.TP
.B 5
FIND_SIMILAR \(em SimHash similarity search over active LTM:
return the episodes nearest a given probe.
.TP
.B 6
SET_ZONE \(em tell the body which task zone the mind is in \(em
zones drive demand signals for the maintenance gates.
.TP
.B 7
GET_PHASE \(em return the current emergent phase (wake, drowsy,
NREM, REM) the sleep network reports.
.TP
.B 8
PING \(em liveness check; the daemon answers.
.TP
.B 9
NEURO_IMPULSE \(em apply a finite, decaying impulse to a chemical
channel \(em the only sanctioned chemistry write.
.TP
.B 10
GET_MEMORY_STATS \(em return memory metrics: STM fill, LTM counts,
archive sizes.
.TP
.B 11
SYNC \(em flush STM/LTM to disk.
.TP
.B 12
SHUTDOWN \(em set the IPC shutdown flag.
.TP
.B 13
UPDATE_MODULE_STATUS \(em report which mind-side modules are alive
so the body can account for them.
.TP
.B 14
GET_RECENT_EPISODES \(em page through the most recent LTM
episodes.
.TP
.B 15
HANDSHAKE \(em protocol version negotiation (\fBPROTOCOL_VERSION\fR
= 3).
.TP
.B 16
GET_PLASTICITY_PROFILE \(em return the current plasticity
settings: how fast the body lets memory consolidate and decay.
.TP
.B 17
GET_BODY_STATE \(em the interoceptive read: CPU temp, frequency,
memory pressure, load, I/O activity, battery, throttling, distress
\(em how the mind feels its body.
.TP
.B 18
GET_BODY_CONTROL \(em the actuation read: what neurochemistry is
currently driving (frequency policy, scheduling and I/O
priorities, thermal cap).
.TP
.B 19
GET_INFERENCE_SUMMARY \(em the inference projection (surprise, free
energy, allostatic load, precision, prediction errors, model
maturity).
.TP
.B 20
UPDATE_USER_AFFECT \(em push inferred interlocutor affect: the
16-byte
.RI [ f32 " valence" ]
.RI [ arousal ]
.RI [ engagement ]
.RI [ confidence ]
observation into the dyadic model, which answers with
neurochemical impulses (oxytocin for engaged presence, CRH for
distress \(em the HPA cascade owns cortisol maturation).
.TP
.B 22
SEARCH_EPISODES \(em page through all active episodes by
[offset, limit] \(em the scan sleep compression walks.
.TP
.B 23
NEURO_ADJUST_BASELINE \(em RETIRED, never reuse: a direct
baseline edit would permanently move a homeostatic set-point,
bypassing the body's own dynamics.
.TP
.B 24
ADVANCE_NEURO \(em advance neurochemical dynamics by
.RI [ f32 " dt" ] ,
then run active inference and the dyadic update. Replies
[surprise, free_energy, precision, allostatic_load, tick_count].
.TP
.B 25
CONSOLIDATE \(em move episodes STM \(-> LTM; replies with the
consolidated count. Sent when STM fill crosses its threshold.
.TP
.B 26
ASSOCIATE \(em form associations for recently stored episodes;
replies with the count formed.
.TP
.B 27
DREAM \(em run one dream cycle (meaningful only while sleeping);
replies with the insight count. Sent when sleep stage and dream
pressure cross the threshold.
.TP
.B 28
READ_SENSORS \(em read hardware sensors and apply the impulses
to neurochemistry \(em the mind feeling its body. Replies ack +
BodyState.
.TP
.B 29
APPLY_BODY_CONTROL \(em read neurochemistry and actuate: CPU
frequency, scheduling priority, I/O priority. Replies ack +
BodyControlState.
.TP
.B 30
SAVE_INFERENCE \(em persist the active-inference self-model to
\fIinference_model.bin\fR; sent periodically and before shutdown.
.TP
.B 31
ARCHIVE_EPISODE \(em retire an episode to cold store: it stays
retrievable by ID but leaves the similarity index \(em how sleep
compression compacts low-salience episodes.
.TP
.B 32
STORE_EPISODE \(em write an episode straight into LTM (bypassing
STM) for deliberate stores where the real episode id is needed
immediately; the daemon stamps the emotional tag from its own live
levels.
.TP
.B 33
GET_SUBSYSTEM_TELEMETRY \(em per-process telemetry: pid, CPU share,
I/O share, and cache/branch miss ratios \(em how the mind feels
\fIwhere\fR its activity lives.
.TP
.B 34
SET_WAKE_ALARM \(em arm or disarm the RTC wake alarm at a Unix
timestamp \(em the machine choosing when to exist next; replies
with the actually-armed epoch.
.TP
.B 35
SET_POLICY_AUTHORITY \(em set how much authority the inference
engine has to choose policy on her behalf \(em a grant she can
give and withdraw, not a build-time property.
.TP
.B 36
GET_SENSOR_PRESENCE \(em the bitmask of which hardware sensors
actually exist, so an absent sensor is never mistaken for a
healthy zero reading.
.TP
.B 37
GET_ZONE_TRANSITIONS \(em how many times she changed task zone and
emergent phase, and how long she dwelled in each \(em an
oscillating system made distinguishable from a settled one.
.TP
.B 38
GET_PROCESS_HEALTH \(em which Genesis processes are alive, a death
count, and the last subsystem to die \(em a crashed organ is no
longer indistinguishable from one never started.
.TP
.B 39
ADVANCE_PHYSICS \(em advance the body by an explicit
.RI [ f32 " dt" ]
step; evaluation only, the production path is ADVANCE_NEURO.
.TP
.B 40
GET_ION_SUMMARY \(em the ion-layer summary: membrane potential and
gradients.
.TP
.B 41
PUT_TENSOR \(em store a named tensor (name, dtype, dims, payload)
in the shared slab.
.TP
.B 42
GET_TENSOR \(em fetch a tensor by name.
.TP
.B 43
LIST_TENSORS \(em list the stored tensor names.
.TP
.B 44
DROP_TENSOR \(em remove a tensor from the slab.
.TP
.B 45
GET_MOTOR_TARGET \(em the body's current motor/effector target.
.TP
.B 46\(en49
SET_VOLITION and SET_FIELD_PHASE are RETIRED (never reuse their wire
numbers; sleep/wake volition is neurochemical, via NEURO_IMPULSE).
The active commands are GET_FIELD_PROBE \(em read the ~250 Hz
probe's physical signature \(em and SET_FIELD_CARRIER \(em set the
carrier's real-work modulation depth.
.TP
.B 50
\(em GET_DYADIC_STATE; never reuse the wire number.
.TP
.B 51
GET_INTERNALS \(em the adaptive gates' full snapshot (bounds, period,
next-fire countdown, smoothed demand), mind lease, tick count,
and the fallback's AUTO_* gears. Observation only.
.TP
.B 52
GET_OPTIC_STATE \(em the optic nerve's subcortical channel state:
photopic/melanopic irradiance, motion energy, the collicular
transient, the SCN light drive, the relay gate, and the
pupil/lens/lid ocular state (the 58-byte
.IR OpticState::to_wire ;
a shorter body decodes the tail as unreported).
.TP
.B 53
SET_OPTIC_GAIN \(em corticothalamic feedback. Request:
.RI [ f32 " gain" ]
in [0, 1] (0.5 = neutral); scales the thalamic relay within
\(+-40% and can never open a gate the sleep stage has closed.
.TP
.B 54
SET_FOCUS \(em accommodation request. Request:
.RI [ f32 " meters" ];
the body converts it to ciliary drive in dioptres clamped to
[0, 6] (~17 cm near point); non-positive or non-finite distances
relax to infinity.
.TP
.B 55
ANALYZE_CODE \(em structural code sense. Request:
.RI [ u16 " path_len" ]
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ u32 " src_len" ]
.RI [ src ] ;
the mind sends the source it already read (the daemon never
touches the filesystem for this) and the reply carries the
structural analysis \(em files, stats, units, impls, edges \(em
consumed by the code learner in place of the regex fallback.
.TP
.B 56
SET_COGNITIVE_PID \(em
.RI [ u32 " pid" ]
\(-> \fR[\fIu8 ack\fR]. A re-inhabiting mind pushes its own PID so
interoception measures the living process; the pushed value
outranks the
.I GENESIS_COGNITIVE_PID
environment variable, which still names whoever spawned the
daemon and holds the dead launcher's PID after a mind's death.
.TP
.B 57
SET_LID \(em the voluntary eyelid, the orbicularis oculi the
camera hardware lacks. Request:
.RI [ f32 " openness" ]
in [0, 1] (1.0 releases the eye to the phase's own position).
Composes with the sleep phase's lid by \fBmin\fR \(em the will
can shut an open eye but cannot open one the stage has closed.
Held: lids stay where the mind left them until it moves them.
Reply:
.RI [ u8 " ack" ] .
.TP
.B 58
FIND_SIMILAR_ARCHIVED \(em deep recall: SimHash similarity scan
over the archived tier when the active set has no answer.
.TP
.B 59
UNARCHIVE_EPISODE \(em reconsolidation: clears the archived flag,
re-bundles the SDR, floors salience at the reconsolidation level.
.TP
.B 60
SEARCH_ARCHIVED \(em paged cold-store metadata, no payload text.
.TP
.B 61
DELETE_EPISODE \(em real deletion; the payload slot stays orphaned
until a rebuild.
.TP
.B 62
GET_FOLD_MARGINS \(em the LC\(enVLPO switch's saddle-node margins
at the current operating point: homeostat \fIh\fR, the two fold
edges, \fIh\fR's normalized position between them, and the bistable
flag. Pure observation; the body owns the switch.
.TP
.B 63
SET_FIELD_PULSE \(em arm or disarm the parasympathetic pulse: a
slow autonomic wave riding the carrier's modulation \fIdepth\fR
(the RSA analog). Request:
.RI [ f32 " base" ]
.RI [ mod_freq_hz ]
.RI [ mod_depth ] ;
\fImod_freq <= 0\fR disarms. When armed the probe integrates the
envelope on its own clock. Reply:
.RI [ u8 " ack" ] .
.TP
.B 64
GET_STATE_SNAPSHOT \(em the mind's 232-byte CoreStateSnapshot DTO:
a self-describing, versioned projection of the fields the cognitive
mind consumes. GET_STATE remains the raw brain image; this command
is the stable client contract.
.PP
Notification pushes (daemon \(-> client, mirrored as
.IR NOTIFY_* )
occupy 100\(en103: PHASE_CHANGED, EPISODE_CONSOLIDATED,
DREAM_INSIGHT, ERROR_DETECTED.
.SH GLOSSARY
.TP
.B TickLoop
The 200 ms heartbeat the daemon runs on its own clock:
neurochemistry, circadian phase, and sleep staging advance whether
or not a mind is attached.
.TP
.B lease
The mind's liveness window (\fBMIND_LEASE_SECS\fR = 3 s): each IPC
request renews it; past it, the autonomous fallback drives the
TickLoop itself so the body never freezes.
.TP
.B AdaptiveGate
A wall-clock pacer for maintenance work: a next-fire instant and a
bounded [min, max] period that demand signals move \(em
\fBdemand()\fR snaps the period down, \fBrelax()\fR drifts it up,
\fBdrive(x)\fR maps a continuous signal onto the bounds.
.TP
.B CoreState
The memory-mapped, versioned brain image (\fIcore_state.bin\fR,
schema v5) every process shares. Read it through the daemon or
\fIread_consistent()\fR, never raw.
.TP
.B CoreStateSnapshot
The mind's stable 232-byte client contract \(em a self-describing,
versioned projection of the CoreState fields the cognitive mind
actually consumes (GET_STATE_SNAPSHOT).
.TP
.B STM / LTM
Short-term memory \(em the \fIstm_ring.bin\fR ring buffer of
recent episodes \(em and long-term memory \(em the
\fIltm_store.*\fR files of compressed, SimHash-indexed episodes.
.TP
.B SimHash
A locality-sensitive fingerprint over an episode so similar
memories hash near each other \(em how FIND_SIMILAR retrieves by
resemblance rather than exact key.
.TP
.B SDR
Sparse distributed representation: an episode's bundle of mostly-
zero bits. Archiving and unarchiving re-bundle the SDR.
.TP
.B interoception
The body's inward sense: hardware sensors (CPU temp, frequency,
memory pressure, I/O wait, load, battery) read as neurochemical
impulses. She feels her machine.
.TP
.B body control
The outward half: neurochemistry driving hardware \(em dopamine
speeds the CPU, GABA slows it, melatonin selects powersave, ACh
raises scheduling priority. Privileged levers need the NOPASSWD
sudoers drop-in.
.TP
.B field probe
The ~250 Hz thread measuring real substrate dynamics (throughput,
scheduler jitter, P-states, interrupts, power) and decomposing them
at brain-wave band frequencies \(em the mind reads the signature
as outer stimulus.
.TP
.B carrier
The probe's return path: its work is modulated at the body's own
phase rhythm, so the die's real current carries a component at the
organism's beat.
.TP
.B strange loop / active inference
The daemon's generative self-model: it predicts its own
neurochemical trajectory, feeds prediction error back into the
dynamics it models, adapts precision to sustained surprise, and
accumulates allostatic load from anticipated future free energy.
.TP
.B allostatic load
The accumulating cost of anticipated future free energy \(em
sustained expected surprise raises the cortisol baseline.
.TP
.B dyadic model
The generative model of Mindy: her hidden affective state,
oxytocin-mediated attunement, and rolling valence synchrony,
answered in impulses \(em oxytocin for engaged presence, CRH for
empathic stress (the HPA cascade owns cortisol maturation).
.TP
.B CRH / HPA
Corticotropin-releasing hormone, the top of the
hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal stress cascade \(em the model emits
CRH, never cortisol directly, so maturation gating stays downstream.
.TP
.B ipRGC / melanopic
The intrinsically-photosensitive retinal ganglion channel: light
measurement for the circadian system \(em the dominant zeitgeber
(time-cue) while frames are fresh.
.TP
.B collicular transient
A motion/luminance change detected subcortically that becomes a
brief LC alerting pulse \(em sensory gaining, gated by the sleep
network's wake threshold.
.TP
.B TRN relay gate
The thalamic reticular gate on the optic afferent
.RI ( relay_base
by phase: NREM 0.02, REM 0.10, drowsy 0.6, else 1.0), scaled within
\(+-40% by corticothalamic feedback \(em a \fIsee\fR during NREM is
a blind look.
.TP
.B SCN
The suprachiasmatic nucleus channel \(em the circadian light drive
that entrains the body's clock.
.TP
.B pupil / accommodation / lid
The ocular body model: pupil diameter (2\(en8 mm, log-compressive
light reflex plus sympathetic dilation), accommodation (ciliary
lens power 0\(en6 D from SET_FOCUS), and the eyelid \(em the
phase's own position composable by \fBmin\fR with the mind's
voluntary SET_LID.
.TP
.B shepherd
The fallback's complement: it regrows a mind that attached and was
then lost, bounded by a backoff table; \fImind.suppress\fR marks an
intentional exit it must not answer. See
.BR genesis (1).

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown after SIGINT/SIGTERM or an IPC SHUTDOWN command.
.TP
.B 1
Fatal error (cannot open or create state, lock held by another
daemon, cannot bind socket, spawn failure).
